  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many bags of chips Abie has in the end, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Start with the initial number of bags of chips Abie had.\n2. Subtract the number of bags she gave to her friend.\n3. Add the number of bags she bought in the store.\n\nLet's go through the steps in detail:\n\n1. Abie initially had 20 bags of chips.\n2. She gave 4 bags to her friend. So, we subtract 4 from 20:\n   \\[\n   20 - 4 = 16\n   \\]\n   Now, Abie has 16 bags of chips.\n3. She then bought another 6 bags of chips. So, we add 6 to 16:\n   \\[\n   16 + 6 = 22\n   \\]\n   Now, Abie has 22 bags of chips.\n\nTherefore, the final number of bags of chips Abie has is \\boxed{22}.",
